<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FlexiPage xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>decorate</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;As a result of Project Dawn findings in an audit of Direct Tenders, our OEMs are expected to provide complete details and information about the tender, which may require a Request for Proposal (RFP) or Request for Quote (RFQ). Sales and Pricing are expected to review tender requests for high quality, complete, detailed information about the request, including filling in all comments, and ensuring any RFP or RFQ required is attached to the request. If tender requests are not complete and do not provide justification, Sales and Pricing should either send the request back to the OEM or reject the request. If any portion of the tender request seems odd or suspicious, please contact Corporate Security (DealValidation@intel.com) for assistance in investigating the request. If you see something, say something!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End Customer must be Unified to update quote line to Won!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When a quote is submitted using Write In End Customer, the end customer must be validated through the unification process by the UCD team. The UCD team may require additional information about the end customer, like a physical address or URL, to complete the unification process. The team will email the AE, if available on the quote, or the SDM directly requesting additional information about the end customer. If you receive an email from central.customer.data.operations@intel.com asking for clarification about an end customer, it is imperative you respond as quickly as possible. If the UCD team does not get a response within 30 days, they will stop the unification process, which will prevent the quote line from being marked as Won and will delay any rebate payment on the request. If you need to retrigger the unification process, please email My.Deals.Support@intel.com.&lt;/p&gt;</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>flexipage:richText</componentName>
                <identifier>flexipage_richText</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
